  {
   "evidence": "`div_mul_eq_mul_div : a / b * c = a * c / b` (`upstream/mathlib/Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Basic.lean:567`) rewrites the RHS `I / I' * F` to `I * F / I'`, matching the LHS produced by `rw [h]`; `rw` only attempts `rfl` after the whole rule list, so the redundant step is not an error.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Nuclear/Medium/NuclearEffect.lean",
   "fix": "Drop the trailing `mul_comm`, or make the step robust: `rw [h'.finalState_eq_div hI', h]; ring`.",
   "issue": "`rw [h'.finalState_eq_div hI', h, div_mul_eq_mul_div, mul_comm]` ends with an argument-free `mul_comm`. After `div_mul_eq_mul_div` the goal is already `I * F / I' = I * F / I'`, so `mul_comm` only permutes the same instance on both sides; it is dead weight whose matched instance depends on kabstract's traversal order.",
